{
  "experiment": "qwen-politi-finetune-v1",
  "status": "intermediate",
  "question": "Can a 0.5B-1.5B causal LM recover PolitiFact's 6-way ordinal rating from the claim text alone?",
  "scoring": {
    "test": "First line of the generation, then the longest PolitiFact label that is a prefix of that line. Unrecognized strings count as incorrect for accuracy. MAE, within-1, macro-F1 on covered, and quadratic kappa use recognized predictions only.",
    "ordinal_scale": [
      "pants-fire",
      "false",
      "mostly-false",
      "half-true",
      "mostly-true",
      "true"
    ],
    "validation": "Teacher-forced argmax over label-token positions. macro_f1 and cohen_kappa are computed only on strings that exactly match a label (recognized_ratio). Do not compare that macro_f1 to test accuracy."
  },
  "notes": [
    "There is no zero-shot Qwen2.5-1.5B run. The matched before/after comparison is the 0.5B pair. The 1.5B numbers are the tuned model only.",
    "Every test metric is aligned to data/test.json (4231 statements). For the zero-shot 0.5B file, only the first recorded prediction per statement is used; later appended passes are excluded.",
    "Train-time eval_macro_f1 is computed only on recognized validation labels.",
    "Tuned 1.5B generations usually continue after the label (for example 'mostly-false' then a newline and 'statement'). Exact string match on that file scores about 0.012. The test figures use prefix parsing.",
    "Adapters, checkpoints, and raw prediction dumps are local only."
  ],
